<p>A good <strong>beef barbecue</strong> benefits from combining cuts with different thickness, fat and texture. This makes it easier to cook in stages and serve a wider range of preferences.</p>
<p>The selection includes skirt steak, ribs, picanha, flank, tomahawk, rib steak and a dedicated barbecue box.</p>
{{PRODUCTS}}
<h2>Quick-cooking barbecue cuts</h2><p>Skirt steak and thinner rib cuts cook quickly and are useful for the first rounds from the grill.</p>
<h2>Thick sharing steaks</h2><p>Tomahawk and rib steak need more control. Their thickness allows a strong exterior sear followed by gentler finishing and a proper resting period.</p>
<h2>Picanha and flank</h2><p>Both are classic grilling cuts, but their fat and fibre structure call for different handling and slicing.</p>
<h2>Barbecue boxes</h2><p>If you prefer a ready-made selection, the barbecue box combines several products in one order.</p>
